      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand how tempting it feels to try and fix things by stepping away, but leaving your child to deal with complicated emotions about your illness would likely create far more confusion and pain for them in the long run. Your presence, even while you feel broken, is the only stable anchor they have for understanding what they are going through. Stepping away would not simplify their life; it would deepen their own burdens by removing the person they love most and leaving them with unanswered questions. Your role is to witness their journey through this together, and no matter how heavy the weight feels right now, you are the one who can help them carry it.",
